---
title: Big Mac
servings: 4
course: Main
prep time: 20m
cook time: 15m
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: American
---

= Sauce =

To make the burger sauce add @mayonnaise{50%g}, @shallots{30%g}(finely diced), @dill pickles{30%g}(finely diced), @tomato ketchup{40%g}, @French mustard{15%g}, @onion powder{0.5%tsp}, @garlic powder{0.5%tsp}, @sweet paprika{0.5%tsp}, and @white wine vinegar{1%tsp} into a bowl and mix. Refrigerate for ~refrigerate{1%hour} for the flavours to combine.

= Burger =

In a separate bowl, season the @beef mince{400%g} with @salt and @pepper and form into eight 50 g balls. Press into a 12 cm ring mould to form a thin pattie.

Place the @white onion{0.5}(diced) into ice cold water. Leave for ~onion{10%minutes} and then drain.

Heat a #large frying pan{} over medium heat and then lightly toast the @seeded burger buns{8}. Put to one side. Add @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} to the pan and fry the burgers in two batches, cooking for ~burger{2%minutes} per side, until cooked. Place a piece of @American cheese{4%slices} on four of the patties  for the final minute to allow it to melt a little.

To assemble the burgers, spread some burger sauce across the bottom bun. Sprinkle over some of the crisped onions and @iceberg lettuce{0.25%head}(finely shredded) then add one burger pattie. Top with the second base, more burger sauce, onions and lettuce and @dill pickles{2}(finely sliced). Finally, top with the second burger patty and bun top.

> Serve with classic fries and a can of coke.